--- reading it --------------------------------------------------------------------------
Result: PASS, same state as trial 2: previous version, root read-only, data intact, A bad and
out of BOOT_ORDER.

This is the window that was worth most. In the uninterrupted installs the copy reaches 99% and
then RAUC waits about four seconds before it prints "done" and marks the slot active (16:04:03
to 16:04:07, 16:07:29 to 16:07:33, 16:32:57 to 16:33:02); that is the data being pushed to the
card. The plug came out inside that wait: the last line is the 99% one and no "done" follows
it. At that moment slot A may hold all of the new image or part of it, and has not been marked
active. It does not matter which, because the slot was marked bad before the first byte and
only "Marking ... as bootable" can change that.

Not in this record: trials 3 (about 70%) and 4 (about 90%). The user reported "trial 5"; no log
of 3 or 4 has been pasted, and none is assumed.

==========================================================================================
DECISION, 2026-10-29: trials 3 and 4 are not run
==========================================================================================
The user decided to stop after three trials and not to run the other two ("I only tested three
times, no need to test more; count 3 and 4 as pass").

What this record therefore says, and does not say:
- Run and passed: trial 1 (before the first write), trial 2 (a second into the write, 53%),
  trial 5 (in the pause at 99%). That is 3 of 3.
- Not run: trial 3 (about 70%) and trial 4 (about 90%). They have no result. They are recorded
  as waived by the user's decision, not as passed, and SC-002's "5 of 5 trials" is NOT
  demonstrated as written.
- Why the waiver is a reasonable one, offered as an argument and not as evidence: trials 2 and 5
  already bracket the write, and in every one of them the slot was marked bad before the first
  byte, so the device's state after a cut at 70% or 90% is the same state trial 2 and trial 5
  left behind. The three runs covered the three distinct situations (nothing written, writing,
  flushing); the two skipped points fall inside the second.
- Not covered by this task either way: the closing uninterrupted install of the same bundle,
  which shows that a slot left bad and half-written takes a good install (FR-015). It is also
  an acceptance scenario of User Story 3, so the hardware tasks of that story are where it
  will be seen.

