--- reading it --------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. FR-015 holds. A slot recorded bad, and left half-written by the cut trials, became eligible
   again on the next trusted install (BOOT_ORDER "A B", BOOT_A_LEFT=3, status good), booted,
   and confirmed itself. The version it reports is the older bundle's, 40a54ec, which tells it
   apart from slot B (1c7e147), so what booted is what was just written and not leftover content.
2. The pre-install handler did not get in the way: with nothing pending (slot B running and
   primary) it let the install through, which is what a recovering device needs.
3. A consequence of the clock rule, worth knowing and not a defect: the floor is the running
   image's build time, so booting an OLDER image lowers it. The clock here went from slot B's
   floor (2026-10-29 09:15:01) to slot A's (08:46:19), half an hour back. A certificate issued
   between those two times would be "not yet valid" on the older slot. The development signing
   certificate dates from 2026-10-28 05:31, so nothing here is affected; research R8 already
   records that a certificate issued after the running image was built is the one gap.
4. Boot time, coarse: the reboot banner at 17:54:41 to the login prompt at 17:54:53 is about 12 s
   with one-second timestamps, against a budget of 12.65 s. Closer than the 11 s of the earlier
   capture; T043 must measure it with grabserial, three runs, before anything is claimed.
